From 912ea119524c1f9fac4b7da7892d54f493e54ca7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dario Gabriel Lipicar <dario@status.im>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:06:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(network): report each dial and the addresses peers
 gossip

A client that picks its own peers could not tell which of them answered:
the warnings for a failed or timed-out connection name no peer, and with
whitelist_only no peer is asked for addresses. Builder::report_peers has
the node report how each dial ends, as Info::Dial with the peer's address
and port: its version's services and protocol version, timed out, refused,
unreachable, or failed on this side. It also asks each peer for addresses
(getaddr), with whitelist_only too, and reports every addrv2 message as
Info::Addresses with its sender. A failed TCP or SOCKS5 connect keeps its
cause: a SOCKS5 reply speaks of the destination, while a proxy that can't
be reached says nothing about the peer. Out of peers to dial, the node
waits for the handshakes in flight before it gives up, so each of them
reports too. Off by default.
